    {
      "id": "02-create",
      "instruction": "In Odoo (already logged in as admin), go to the Sales app and create a new quotation for the customer '{{runid}} Bench Customer' (the customer field is an autocomplete dropdown - type the name and click the matching option from the dropdown). Add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (the product field is an autocomplete dropdown - type a few letters and click an actual option from the dropdown), set the quantity to 3. Save the quotation. Then report: (a) the exact product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that line, (c) the untaxed amount the app computes in the totals section, and (d) the quotation reference/name (e.g. S00042). Read these values back from the saved page to verify.",
      "outputs": [
        "product_name",
        "quantity",
        "unit_price",
        "tax",
        "line_tax_excl_total",
        "customer",
        "customer_city",
        "quotation_reference",
        "save_blocked_by"
      ],
